text: ['As Canker Abomination enters the battlefield, choose an opponent. Canker Abomination enters the battlefield with a -1/-1 counter on it for each creature that player controls.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, destroy target creature with a -1/-1 counter on it.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, return a permanent you control to its owner's hand.", "Cast this spell only if you've cast another green spell this turn.\\nTrample", 'Change the text of target spell or permanent by replacing all instances of one color word with another.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', 'Chaotic Backlash deals damage to target player equal to twice the number of white and/or blue permanents they control.', "Choose any number of target creatures. Each of those creatures gains persist until end of turn. (When it dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Chroma — Each creature you control gets +1/+1 for each white mana symbol in its mana cost.', "Chroma — Reveal any number of cards in your hand. You gain 2 life for each green mana symbol in those cards' mana costs.", 'Chroma — Reveal the top ten cards of your library. For each blue mana symbol in the mana costs of the revealed cards, target opponent mills a card. Then put the cards you revealed this way on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Chroma — Umbra Stalker's power and toughness are each equal to the number of black mana symbols in the mana costs of cards in your graveyard.", 'Chroma — When Outrage Shaman enters the battlefield, it deals damage to target creature equal to the number of red mana symbols in the mana costs of permanents you control.', 'Chroma — When Springjack Shepherd enters the battlefield, create a 0/1 white Goat creature token for each white mana symbol in the mana costs of permanents you control.', "Chroma — {2}, Sacrifice a creature: Fiery Bombardment deals damage to any target equal to the number of red mana symbols in the sacrificed creature's mana cost.", 'Counter target spell. Its controller draws a card.\\nDraw a card.', 'Create a 1/1 black and green Worm creature token for each land card in your graveyard.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', 'Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', 'Create a 5/5 blue and red Elemental creature token with flying.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', "Create a token that's a copy of target creature.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)", 'Create two 1/1 white Kithkin Soldier creature tokens.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', 'Creatures your opponents control get -1/-0 until end of turn if {U} was spent to cast this spell, and creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn if {R} was spent to cast this spell. (Do both if {U}{R} was spent.)', 'Creatures your opponents control lose flying until end of turn if {G} was spent to cast this spell, and creatures you control gain flying until end of turn if {U} was spent to cast this spell. (Do both if {G}{U} was spent.)', 'Defender, flying\\nWhenever you cast a white spell, Loyal Gyrfalcon loses defender until end of turn.', 'Destroy target land. You gain 2 life.', "Destroy target nongreen creature. Its controller loses 3 life if you've cast another black spell this turn.", 'Double strike', "Each opponent who controls more creatures than you can't cast creature spells. The same is true for artifacts and enchantments.\\nEach opponent who controls more lands than you can't play lands.", 'Each player returns each creature card from their graveyard to the battlefield with an additional -1/-1 counter on it.', 'Enchant creature\\nAs long as enchanted creature is black, it gets +1/+1 and has deathtouch. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy that creature.)\\nAs long as enchanted creature is green, it gets +1/+1 and all creatures able to block it do so.', "Enchant creature\\nAs long as enchanted creature is blue, it gets +1/+1 and has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\nAs long as enchanted creature is red, it gets +1/+1 and has haste.", 'Enchant creature\\nAs long as enchanted creature is green, it gets +1/+1 and has vigilance.\\nAs long as enchanted creature is blue, it gets +1/+1 and has flying.', 'Enchant creature\\nAs long as enchanted creature is red, it gets +1/+1 and has "{R/W}: This creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn."\\nAs long as enchanted creature is white, it gets +1/+1 and has lifelink. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Enchant creature\\nAs long as enchanted creature is white, it gets +1/+2.\\nAs long as enchanted creature is black, it gets +2/+1.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may gain 1 life.", 'Exile target card from a graveyard. Create a 1/1 white and black Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Exile target creature.', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Fire at Will deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three target attacking or blocking creatures.', 'First strike\\nBelligerent Hatchling enters the battlefield with four -1/-1 counters on it.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Belligerent Hatchling.\\nWhenever you cast a white spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Belligerent Hatchling.', 'Flame Jab deals 1 damage to any target.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', "Flash\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Flying, first strike', 'Flying, lifelink\\nDivinity of Pride gets +4/+4 as long as you have 25 or more life.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may gain control of target permanent until end of turn. If you do, untap it and it gains haste until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nAttacking creatures you control get +2/+0.', 'Flying\\nBloodied Ghost enters the battlefield with a -1/-1 counter on it.', "Flying\\nEvershrike gets +2/+2 for each Aura attached to it.\\n{X}{W/B}{W/B}: Return Evershrike from your graveyard to the battlefield. You may put an Aura card with mana value X or less from your hand onto the battlefield attached to it. If you don't, exile Evershrike.", 'Flying\\nWhen Archon of Justice dies, exile target permanent.', "Flying\\nWhen Dream Thief enters the battlefield, draw a card if you've cast another blue spell this turn.", "Flying\\nWhen Flickerwisp enters the battlefield, exile another target permanent. Return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Flying\\nWhenever a player casts a nonblack spell, that player loses 1 life.', 'Flying\\nWither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nWhenever Needle Specter deals combat damage to a player, that player discards that many cards.', "Flying\\nYou have hexproof. (You can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", "Flying\\n{1}{W}, Sacrifice Kithkin Spellduster: Destroy target enchantment.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Flying\\n{U/R}: Talonrend gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', "Flying\\n{U}, Sacrifice Glen Elendra Archmage: Counter target noncreature spell.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Flying\\n{U}: Target permanent becomes blue in addition to its other colors until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{W/B}{W/B}{W/B}: Regenerate target creature.', 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gets +X/+0 and gains haste until end of turn.', 'Haste\\nChroma — When Heartlash Cinder enters the battlefield, it gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the number of red mana symbols in the mana costs of permanents you control.', "Haste\\nHotheaded Giant enters the battlefield with two -1/-1 counters on it unless you've cast another red spell this turn.", "Haste\\nThunderblust has trample as long as it has a -1/-1 counter on it.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'If {B} was spent to cast this spell, you may have target creature get -3/-3 until end of turn. If {G} was spent to cast this spell, you may have target creature get +3/+3 until end of turn. (Do both if {B}{G} was spent.)', "Indestructible\\nWhenever Sapling of Colfenor attacks, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, you gain life equal to that card's toughness, lose life equal to its power, then put it into your hand.", "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nWhenever Cold-Eyed Selkie deals combat damage to a player, you may draw that many cards.", 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', 'Lifelink\\nVoracious Hatchling enters the battlefield with four -1/-1 counters on it.\\nWhenever you cast a white spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Voracious Hatchling.\\nWhenever you cast a black spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Voracious Hatchling.', "Nettle Sentinel doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nWhenever you cast a green spell, you may untap Nettle Sentinel.", "Noggle Bandit can't be blocked except by creatures with defender.", 'Noxious Hatchling enters the battlefield with four -1/-1 counters on it.\\nWither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nWhenever you cast a black spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Noxious Hatchling.\\nWhenever you cast a green spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Noxious Hatchling.', 'Other black creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nOther green creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may create a 1/1 black and green Worm creature token.', 'Other blue creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nOther red creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{U/R}{U/R}{U/R}{U/R}: You may put a blue or red creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', "Other green creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nOther blue creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nUntap all green and/or blue creatures you control during each other player's untap step.", 'Other red creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nOther white creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, Balefire Liege deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\nWhenever you cast a white spell, you gain 3 life.', "Other white creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nOther black creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever you cast a white spell, you may tap target creature.\\nWhenever you cast a black spell, you may destroy target creature if it's tapped.", "Overbeing of Myth's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.\\nAt the beginning of your draw step, draw an additional card.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn if {W} was spent to cast this spell. Each player loses 1 life for each attacking creature they control if {B} was spent to cast this spell. (Do both if {W}{B} was spent.)', 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt to you and permanents you control this turn.', 'Protection from white and from black\\n{W/B}: Stillmoon Cavalier gains flying until end of turn.\\n{W/B}: Stillmoon Cavalier gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{W/B}{W/B}: Stillmoon Cavalier gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Put all creatures on the bottom of their owners' libraries.", 'Rekindled Flame deals 4 damage to any target.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if an opponent has no cards in hand, you may return Rekindled Flame from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return all nonblue creatures to their owners' hands.", "Sacrifice Aerie Ouphes: It deals damage equal to its power to target creature with flying.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Sacrifice Duergar Assailant: It deals 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', "Search target player's library for up to X cards, where X is the number of Swamps you control, and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", "Shrewd Hatchling enters the battlefield with four -1/-1 counters on it.\\n{U/R}: Target creature can't block Shrewd Hatchling this turn.\\nWhenever you cast a blue spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Shrewd Hatchling.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Shrewd Hatchling.", "Shroud (This enchantment can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\n{X}: Put X tower counters on Helix Pinnacle.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if there are 100 or more tower counters on Helix Pinnacle, you win the game.", "Sturdy Hatchling enters the battlefield with four -1/-1 counters on it.\\n{G/U}: Sturdy Hatchling gains shroud until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\nWhenever you cast a green spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Sturdy Hatchling.\\nWhenever you cast a blue spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Sturdy Hatchling.", "Swampwalk, forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp or a Forest.)", "Switch target creature's power and toughness until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.", 'Target creature gains double strike until end of turn. (It deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)', 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', "Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a green or white creature card from it. You gain life equal to that creature card's toughness, then that player discards that card.", "Target player can't play lands this turn if {R} was spent to cast this spell and can't cast creature spells this turn if {W} was spent to cast this spell. (Do both if {R}{W} was spent.)", 'Target player discards a card.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', 'Target player draws a card.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', 'Target player loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample\\nAltar Golem's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures on the battlefield.\\nAltar Golem doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nTap five untapped creatures you control: Untap Altar Golem.", "Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a creature. You gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", "Trample\\nChroma — Primalcrux's power and toughness are each equal to the number of green mana symbols in the mana costs of permanents you control.", 'Trample\\nDeity of Scars enters the battlefield with two -1/-1 counters on it.\\n{B/G}, Remove a -1/-1 counter from Deity of Scars: Regenerate Deity of Scars.', 'Trample\\nTap an untapped red creature you control other than Impelled Giant: Impelled Giant gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the power of the creature tapped this way.', 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.\\nRetrace (You may cast this card from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying its other costs.)', 'Until end of turn, target creature gains "{T}: Return target nonland permanent to its owner\'s hand."', 'Until end of turn, target creature loses all abilities and becomes a green Snake with base power and toughness 1/1.\\nDraw a card.', 'When Desecrator Hag enters the battlefield, return to your hand the creature card in your graveyard with the greatest power. If two or more cards are tied for greatest power, you choose one of them.', 'When Duergar Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Mountains, you may destroy target artifact.\\nWhen Duergar Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Plains, you may destroy target enchantment.', 'When Endless Horizons enters the battlefield, search your library for any number of Plains cards, exile them, then shuffle.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may put a card you own exiled with Endless Horizons into your hand.', 'When Gwyllion Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Plains, you may create a 1/1 white Kithkin Soldier creature token.\\nWhen Gwyllion Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Swamps, you may put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.', 'When Hag Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Swamps, you may have target player discard a card.\\nWhen Hag Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Forests, you may put target card from your graveyard on top of your library.', 'When Kithkin Zealot enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life for each black and/or red permanent target opponent controls.', 'When Marshdrinker Giant enters the battlefield, destroy target Island or Swamp an opponent controls.', "When Noggle Bridgebreaker enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.", 'When Noggle Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Islands, you may tap two target permanents.\\nWhen Noggle Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Mountains, you may have Noggle Hedge-Mage deal 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'When Noggle Ransacker enters the battlefield, each player draws two cards, then discards a card at random.', 'When Nucklavee enters the battlefield, you may return target red sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.\\nWhen Nucklavee enters the battlefield, you may return target blue instant card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Regal Force enters the battlefield, draw a card for each green creature you control.', 'When Rise of the Hobgoblins enters the battlefield, you may pay {X}. If you do, create X 1/1 red and white Goblin Soldier creature tokens.\\n{R/W}: Red creatures and white creatures you control gain first strike until end of turn.', "When Selkie Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Forests, you may gain 3 life.\\nWhen Selkie Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Islands, you may return target tapped creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Soul Snuffers enters the battlefield, put a -1/-1 counter on each creature.', 'When Tilling Treefolk enters the battlefield, you may return up to two target land cards from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Wistful Selkie enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'Whenever Ashling, the Extinguisher deals combat damage to a player, choose target creature that player controls. The player sacrifices that creature.', 'Whenever Spitemare is dealt damage, it deals that much damage to any target.', 'Whenever a permanent you control becomes untapped, Wake Thrasher gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever you cast a green spell, you may create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.\\nWhenever you cast a blue spell, you may create a 1/1 blue Bird creature token with flying.', "Whenever you cast a spell that's both black and green, Woodlurker Mimic has base power and toughness 4/5 until end of turn and gains wither until end of turn. (It deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)", "Whenever you cast a spell that's both blue and red, Riverfall Mimic has base power and toughness 3/3 until end of turn and can't be blocked this turn.", "Whenever you cast a spell that's both green and blue, Shorecrasher Mimic has base power and toughness 5/3 until end of turn and gains trample until end of turn.", "Whenever you cast a spell that's both red and white, Battlegate Mimic has base power and toughness 4/2 until end of turn and gains first strike until end of turn.", "Whenever you cast a spell that's both white and black, Nightsky Mimic has base power and toughness 4/4 until end of turn and gains flying until end of turn.", 'Whenever you cast a spell, equipped creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\nEquip {2}', 'Wickerbough Elder enters the battlefield with a -1/-1 counter on it.\\n{G}, Remove a -1/-1 counter from Wickerbough Elder: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)', "Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nPuncture Blast deals 3 damage to any target.', "Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nWhenever Stigma Lasher deals damage to a player, that player can't gain life for the rest of the game.", 'Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls with a -1/-1 counter on it dies, you may return that card to the battlefield under your control.', 'Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\n{1}{G}: Twinblade Slasher gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', 'Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\n{2}{R}, {Q}: Hateflayer deals damage equal to its power to any target. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)', 'Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\n{R/W}: Duergar Cave-Guard gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}, Sacrifice a Scarecrow: Draw a card.\\n{4}, {T}: Return target artifact creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{1}{B/G}: Regenerate Odious Trow.', '{1}{R/W}, {Q}: Attacking creatures get +1/+0 until end of turn. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)', '{1}{U/R}{U/R}: Copy target instant or sorcery spell that targets you. You may choose new targets for the copy.', "{1}{U}, {T}: Return target creature with a counter on it to its owner's hand.", '{1}{W}, {Q}: Create a 1/1 white Kithkin Soldier creature token. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)', '{2}: Draw a card if you have no cards in hand.', '{2}: Target black creature gains wither until end of turn. (It deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)', '{2}: Target red creature gains haste until end of turn.', "{2}: Target white creature gains persist until end of turn. (When it dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", '{2}{G/U}, {Q}: Double the number of each kind of counter on target permanent. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)', '{2}{R}, {T}, Put a -1/-1 counter on a creature you control: Hatchet Bully deals 2 damage to any target.', "{3}: Target blue creature gains shroud until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", '{3}: Target green creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{B/G}, Remove a -1/-1 counter from a creature you control: Quillspike gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', '{B/G}{B/G}: Exile target card from a graveyard. You gain 1 life.', "{G/U}, Sacrifice Grazing Kelpie: Put target card from a graveyard on the bottom of its owner's library.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", '{G/U}: Groundling Pouncer gets +1/+3 and gains flying until end of turn. Activate only once each turn and only if an opponent controls a creature with flying.', '{G/U}{G/U}: Target creature you control becomes the color or colors of your choice until end of turn.', '{R/W}: Figure of Destiny becomes a Kithkin Spirit with base power and toughness 2/2.\\n{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}: If Figure of Destiny is a Spirit, it becomes a Kithkin Spirit Warrior with base power and toughness 4/4.\\n{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}: If Figure of Destiny is a Warrior, it becomes a Kithkin Spirit Warrior Avatar with base power and toughness 8/8, flying, and first strike.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Create a 0/1 white Goat creature token.\\n{T}, Sacrifice X Goats: Add X mana of any one color. You gain X life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{B/G}, {T}: Add {B}{B}, {B}{G}, or {G}{G}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{G/U}, {T}: Add {G}{G}, {G}{U}, or {U}{U}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R/W}, {T}: Add {R}{R}, {R}{W}, or {W}{W}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{U/R}, {T}: Add {U}{U}, {U}{R}, or {R}{R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{W/B}, {T}: Add {W}{W}, {W}{B}, or {B}{B}.', '{T}: Cinder Pyromancer deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, you may untap Cinder Pyromancer.', '{T}: For each color among permanents you control, add one mana of that color.', '{T}: Tap target creature.\\nWhenever you cast a white spell, you may untap Ballynock Trapper.', '{T}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.\\nWhenever you cast a blue spell, you may untap Merrow Levitator.', '{T}: Target player exiles a card from their graveyard.\\nWhenever you cast a black spell, you may untap Merrow Bonegnawer.', '{T}: Target red or green creature gets -2/-0 until end of turn.', '{U/R}: Stream Hopper gains flying until end of turn.', "{U/R}: Switch Crag Puca's power and toughness until end of turn.", "{U/R}{U/R}, {T}, Tap two untapped red creatures you control: Crackleburr deals 3 damage to any target.\\n{U/R}{U/R}, {Q}, Untap two tapped blue creatures you control: Return target creature to its owner's hand. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)", "{W/B}{W/B}{W/B}: Restless Apparition gets +3/+3 until end of turn.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)"]
flavor: ['"A great siege is a banquet to him; a long and terrible battle, the most exquisite delicacy."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"Ah, skull of shrew—a very potent substance. In powdered form, it gives thrice the zing of noggle hoof pulp."\\n—Boghald, Barrenton medic', '"Be happy when you see a puca shaped like mischief. It\'s far better than one shaped like death."\\n—Dindun of Kulrath Mine', '"Better for a doun to lose its cenn than its springjacks."', '"Creation is a paradox. It hatches from its opposite."\\n—Olka, Mistmeadow witch', '"Do not linger in such places, child. There the gwyllions dance. If they find you, you will join in their revels for eternity."\\n—Talara, elvish safewright', '"Everything falls apart. But living things fall apart in the most fascinating ways."\\n—Mowagh the Gwyllion', '"Fire\'s out. Should be safe now."\\n—Gnarltrunk', '"For years, the landfolk have emptied their refuse into the waters. It\'s time to return the favor."', '"His skin cuts swords."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"I felt as if I were moving in brackish water, as if I were drowning, even though I knew I stood on dry land."\\n—Dindun of Kulrath Mine', '"I knew a creature carved from a dream of wild freedom. Any attempt to leash or exploit it failed, and at terrible cost."\\n—Ashling', '"I was there to watch my brothers\' quenching. I drew the slightest warmth from their dying rage."\\n—Illulia of Nighthearth', '"I\'d rather hear the screams of battle than the quiet that follows."\\n—Talara, elvish safewright', '"If one gets in your chimney, you\'re going to need a long wick and a barrel of bangstuff to get it out."\\n—Hob Heddil', '"If the whole world burns, I\'ll never grow cold."', '"It\'s always funny till someone gets hurt. Then it\'s hilarious."', '"It\'s not much for eating, but I think we can find somethin\' to do with it."', '"Last time, it tore up the Wilt-Leaf, turned Mistmeadow into a mudhole, and made the river jump its banks. On the bright side, we were eating venison for weeks."\\n—Donal Alloway, cenn of Kinscaer', '"Living scarecrows make a mockery of the natural order. Dead ones make fine hats."', '"Make these shots count. The more foes we drop now, the fewer we\'ll have trying to kill us later."', '"Muscle does not make one strong. It only masks the soul\'s light. True strength lies in purity of purpose."\\n—Donal Alloway, cenn of Kinscaer', '"Nothing is truly your own. It is his, whether you know it or not."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"Only a knife left for a fortnight in the hollow of a ghastbark tree can inflict a wound so grave."\\n—Kithkin superstition', '"She spoke of mystery and portent, of such unfathomable things that my mind screamed for pity."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"She walks among us unseen, learning from our imperfections."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"When in doubt, kill \'em twice."', '"You should see your face right now."', '"Your thoughts betray you."\\n—Illulia of Nighthearth', "A boggart's mind is a tinderbox of volatile thoughts, hungry for a spark.", "A cinder's axe bears no marks from parrying a foe's blade.", "A gwyllion's favorite trap is the vanity mirror. A bewitched piece of glass traps the looker's soul and does away with the body.", 'A mimic need only touch a being to learn its shape, but touching usually leads to mauling and messily eating.', "A mimic's disguise fools its victims just long enough to draw them within range of its venomous tentacles.", 'A river even the merrow dare not cross.', 'After its encounter with the spriggan, the patrol was red with anger, green with envy, white with fear, and painfully black and blue.', 'Anyone who thinks merrows have more brains than brawn has never been run over by one.', 'As he races the moon each night, he draws a glowing equator across the world.', 'As their roots soaked in a weak tea of bogwater and decay, the trees absorbed the essence of death into their living tissue.', 'At full moon, the river seeps over its banks and crawls through the woods like a blanket of serpents.', "Awylla's salvaged dreams would finally be put to good use.", 'Banished to the Dark Meanders for hideous crimes, some merrows find a taste for the darkness . . . and the dead.', 'Beauty is a seed, waiting to blossom under her capable hands.', "Bogles are very tasty if you can get the skin off. It's getting a blade on them that's the problem.", 'Change is a denizen of Shadowmoor as much as ouphes and noggles are.', 'Do the glowing trinkets show it the way home, or do they set a twisted path for someone else to follow?', "Don't venture into the darkness, lest it decide not to let you leave.", 'Duergars are prodigious workers with long memories. Some still fulfill intricately detailed orders given decades, if not centuries, before.', 'Duergars who grow too large to live in the tunnels are sent topside to defend the entrances from intruders.', 'Endry was determined to teach his groundlings a few winged-faerie tricks.', 'Enlightenment is the mundane seen from the vantage point of the divine.', 'Even treefolk witches steer clear of the unpredictable woods near Glen Elendra. Spells refract off the glamer-polished trees and the eyes of lurking pucas.', 'Every skull has a tale to tell, and a skulkin is many dire tales cobbled together.', "Frorn didn't want to be kept, but he didn't want to be thrown back either.", 'Gackt came to regret keeping his pet toads on his head.', "Gnarltrunk didn't remember having quite that many knotholes.", 'He digs his roots into barren ground, searching for old seeds that never had the chance to sprout.', 'He fancies himself a master thief, claiming to "steal the ground" from his victims.', 'Her hunt is silent until a bone snaps or flesh tears. Her victims never know to scream.', 'Her plans may yet bear fruit.', 'Her poppets bring joy to the truly depraved.', 'Hobgoblins are best left alone. They sharpen their farm implements far more than is necessary for their work in the fields.', 'Hobs bury their kin far from home. They believe the dry, open ground keeps hags from stealing the bones and gwyllions from stealing the spirits.', 'In dark times, Truth bears a blade.', 'Inspiration strikes the uncluttered mind.', 'Is her need to heal born out of compassion or penance?', 'It eats and eats until the juiciest morsel it can find is itself.', 'It has no safe side.', 'It hears and answers every orison across Shadowmoor.', 'It hunts with the memory of a long lost herd.', 'It kills two beasts with one thrown.', 'It loathes all tastes but two: spells and flesh.', 'It plucks away memories like choice bits of carrion.', 'It rarely moves, standing stock still in its clearing. When it does stir, ravens stop their cawing and crickets their chirping. All of nature watches in awed silence.', "It's tethered not to keep it from fleeing but to keep it from eating everything in sight.", 'Its wings disturb more than air.', 'Kithkin somnomancers enjoy the peaceful dreams wafting from their victims.', 'Leeches never tire of feeding.', 'Like many who dwell in Shadowmoor now, he was robbed of his better half by the Aurora.', 'Loose earth is not a burial but an appetizer.', 'Losing his possessions distressed him, but the lack of limbs was strangely liberating.', 'Mages dare not attempt magic in its grotesque presence.', 'Many a keen-eared bogle has run afoul of a clever and silently orchestrated kithkin ambush.', "Mimics don't hide their natural form well, but their disguises work well enough on boggarts.", "Mimics don't need perfect disguises. They need only the perfect victims: the naive, the young, or the poor of sight.", 'No matter how large or small, fierce or fleeting, the kithkin have a trap for it.', 'Noggles believe that they were the first race ever to walk Shadowmoor. They don\'t "steal." They just take back what\'s rightfully theirs.', 'Noggles live purely by what they can scavenge. There is not a single thing a noggle eats, wears, or uses that did not once belong to another.', 'Nothing warms the bark on a chilly day like a draught of elf.', 'Once the hideous disease takes hold, it spreads through both bark and mind.', 'Once you have been marked by the merrow, you are not long for their waters.', 'Once your life and all your worldly possessions have been surrendered to her, a gwyllion can be surprisingly civilized.', 'Oona grants her favored subjects a dream from her own guarded heart.', 'Righteous anger hones a humble soul.', 'Selkies call to a sea they never swam, in a tongue they never spoke, with a song they never learned.', "Seyden's temperament didn't take well to the puca's magic. Nor did his face.", 'She follows the old tributaries built when merrows still shaped the tides.', 'She speaks only in vile epithets, spitting out curses and obscenities that harm others just by the hearing.', 'Skulkins confer strange benefits on unsuspecting patrons.', 'Some beasts are born not of a mother, but of magic.', 'Some duergars dismiss the world above as a fable. They react violently when their comfortable illusions are dispelled.', 'Some eat the living. Some eat the dead. It eats the past.', 'Spitting is the customary greeting between a creature and its magical impostor.', 'Suddenly he realized that everything was connected by invisible strings, strings that could be pulled—or cut.', "The Aurora had lessened the kithkins' kindness, deepened their paranoia, and dulled their sense of pain.", 'The Aurora had transformed her into a relentless force of destruction.', "The Aurora replaced the changelings' innocence with malice and their curiosity with hunger.", "The Extinguisher's curse lasted long after her departure.", 'The banner was not a symbol of victory, but a herald of the carnage to come.', "The bogeyman doesn't disappear when you close your eyes.", 'The boggarts gorged themselves until their bellies glowed.', 'The concept of thoughtweft fascinates the Nighthearth cult. Imagine, bringing agony to an entire people by torturing just one.', "The divinity's patronage confers both wicked grace and graceful wickedness.", "The faeries snickered at first. A common hob in Oona's skies? But his lance ended their mockery, and now the sound of a cicada's wings brings a shudder to the faerie heart.", 'The forest grew fangs. The sky spread its wings.', 'The more his flock fears, the more power he wields.', 'The more the scarier.', 'The safewright Talara protects a delicate woodland waterfall. She has vowed to send wave after wave of warriors to slay any who would dare disturb its beauty.', 'The scales of battle rarely balance.', "Their thoughtweft carried Darial's last thoughts back to his doun. They sorely wished it had not.", 'They found themselves alive again, still bearing their mortal wounds.', 'They once sought to unite with the flame of transcendence. Now they seek only to extinguish the lights of others.', 'Thieves know that a snarl in the night means, "Rob another house."', "Though Shadowmoor's monster-haunted wilds beckon, she never leaves her post.", 'Travelers bathe in the falls to wash away curses from the pucas who lurk nearby.', 'Travelers in these waters leave a bit of themselves behind.', 'Trows are the vile trolls that lurk in the bogs of Shadowmoor. They reappear each night to frighten the living and gnaw the dead.', "Trows have learned that it's not wise to eat cinders without a bucket or two of water nearby.", "What the current doesn't take, they do.", 'When a graveyard is full, the gwyllions rattle the tombs and unleash the spirits into the sky.', 'When giants rise from their long slumbers, they rarely remember how fragile the waking world can be.', 'When nature is backed into a corner, just like its children, it lashes out.', "While it's true that a quillspike does heal the sick, it's just because it finds them tastier that way."]
artist: ['Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Carl Frank', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Cole Eastburn', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Dan Seagrave', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Martin', 'Drew Tucker', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Fred Harper', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Howard Lyon', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jason Chan', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Enecio', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'John Franklin Howe', 'Joshua Hagler', 'Kev Walker', 'Larry MacDougall', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paul Bonner', 'Pete Venters', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Whitters', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Brown', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Altmann', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas Denmark', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne Reynolds', "William O'Connor", 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
